Subject: [PATCH 1/2] jails/instances/lab-mail: File posts with Sieve, and
 refuse as Dovecot does
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: pvpzrzlpmwqlqmxquqwmtoqxmsknovso
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:39:12 +0000

Dovecot's LMTP delivers only to INBOX, so the hub needs something to
put a post into lists. Pigeonhole's Sieve does that and keeps the
list's address in Delivered-To, where LMTP's detail mailbox would put
lab-devel+lists@p7x.dev there instead. The spec now names the extra
package, so the implementation adds no software the spec does not
mention.

Dovecot opens a mailbox read-only for a login without write rights. A
STORE or EXPUNGE there answers OK and changes nothing. Only append,
copy, and move answer NO. The rights section and acceptance step 7
said all of them fail, which Dovecot does not do, so a correct build
would fail its own acceptance test.
